    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d223-a6">

                <pb facs="0653" n="439" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg439"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 6.</seg></opener>
                <head>Earl Granville to Lord
                        Lyons</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-10-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 15 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: With reference to your excellency’s
                    dispatch of the 9th instant, I inclose, for your information, a copy of a letter
                    which I have addressed to Count Bernstorff,<anchor n="*" xml:id="d223-f1"/>
                    requesting him to obtain from the King of Prussia permission for the members of
                    Her Majesty’s embassy, together with the servants and other British subjects, to
                    leave Paris.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GRANVILLE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
